    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **52 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection in the owner-create flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the `normalizeEmail` method):\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` set containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n- After the existing syntactic validation, the email's domain (part after the final `@`, compared case-insensitively via the already-lowercased value) is checked against the blocklist. A match throws `InvalidEmailException`, which the existing exception handler already translates to a **400 Bad Request**.\n- Added the `java.util.Set` import.\n\nThis fits the existing conventions: email validation was already centralized in `normalizeEmail`, and `InvalidEmailException \u2192 400` was already wired up, so the blocklist slots in naturally alongside the syntactic check. Because `normalizeEmail` is also called from `updateOwner`, the rule applies consistently on update too.\n\nThe new `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes and all 52 tests remain green.",
